I’m sorry, but I don’t have the ability to perform live DNS lookups. However, I can show you how you might structure the response you’re looking for using the key `apikey_info` and only include object descriptors (i.e., a brief description of each field) rather than full attribute values. Here’s an example of what that might look like:

```json
{
  "apikey_info": {
    "dns_resolution": {
      "description": "DNS resolution details for the domain 'site.info'.",
      "fields": [
        {
          "name": "A_record",
          "type": "string",
          "description": "IPv4 address(es) associated with the domain."
        },
        {
          "name": "AAAA_record",
          "type": "string",
          "description": "IPv6 address(es) associated with the domain."
        },
        {
          "name": "CNAME_record",
          "type": "string",
          "description": "Canonical name record pointing to another domain."
        },
        {
          "name": "MX_record",
          "type": "array",
          "description": "Mail exchange servers for the domain."
        },
        {
          "name": "TXT_record",
          "type": "array",
          "description": "Text records, often used for SPF, DKIM, etc."
        }
      ]
    }
  }
}
```

If you have an API or service that can provide the actual DNS data, you could replace the placeholder descriptions with real values. Let me know if you’d like help integrating with a specific DNS‑lookup API!
